      "id": "perceptron-from-scratch-in-mojo-p8",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "heading": "What Comes Next",
      "text": "A single perceptron can learn AND or OR because each is linearly separable. It cannot learn XOR. That failure is the useful next step: it creates the need for hidden units, multiple decision boundaries, and eventually a small multilayer network built from the same primitive operations.",
